SURFACE DELIVERED (apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/ChartHiddenSeriesContext.*)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Web spec: components/charts/ChartHiddenSeriesContext.tsx — a context bridge that carries
a chart's URL-persisted hidden-series state (hooks/useHiddenSeries.ts → useSearchParams)
to its legend without prop drilling. It is an anonymous module: no titles, no shared
components, no charts/maps, no extracted i18n keys; its only render branches are
`children(null)` (chartKey absent) vs `children(state)` (chartKey present), where the
state is { hidden:Set, toggle, isHidden, reset }.

Native parity files:
  • ChartHiddenSeriesContext.swift          — EnvironmentValues.chartHiddenSeries (createContext/
                                               useContext parity), ChartHiddenSeriesProvider
                                               (conditional inject — children(null)/children(state)),
                                               host surface + consumer (reads the context like the
                                               web ChartLegend reads useChartHiddenSeries()).
  • ChartHiddenSeriesContext.Model.swift     — P1/S8 state holder (useHiddenSeries port:
                                               hidden/toggle/isHidden/reset), ChartHiddenSeriesStore
                                               seam (useSearchParams analogue) + InMemoryHiddenSeriesStore,
                                               P1/S11 view.opened telemetry seam, P1/S10 i18n facade.
  • ChartHiddenSeriesContext.Adapter.swift   — pure: hidden_{chartKey} param name + canonical
                                               sorted-CSV encode/decode (drop-when-empty), projection
                                               (unavailable/empty/active), a11y summaries.
  • ChartHiddenSeriesContext.Views.swift     — header (summary + show-all), series rows (swatch +
                                               eye toggle, strike when hidden), unavailable + empty states.
  • ChartHiddenSeriesContext.Previews.swift  — DEBUG previews: unavailable / empty / all-visible / some-hidden.
  • ChartHiddenSeriesContext.Tests.swift     — XCTest: param, projection, model (toggle/reset/persist/
                                               telemetry/reload), accessibility (co-located per convention).
  • ChartHiddenSeriesContext.strings         — P1/S10 catalog (native consumer chrome; source has no keys).

States reproduced (the web source's real branches; it performs NO async fetch, so the
generic leaf loading/error/stale/offline axes are not applicable and are documented as such):
  • unavailable — chart did not opt in (web context value null). Friendly, never blank.
  • empty       — opted in, no series registered.
  • active      — registered series with per-row show/hide (all-visible / some-hidden / all-hidden).

Build wiring (minimal, disclosed): project.yml adds `TeslaSync/shared-surfaces` to the
TeslaSync + TeslaSync-macOS app-target sources (parallel to feature-views); .swiftlint.yml
adds it to `included`. These mirror how every shared-surface in this batch must be wired.

