ROOT-CAUSE EVIDENCE (pre-existing, OUT OF SCOPE — "other surfaces, each its own prompt")
------------------------------------------------------------------------
My working-tree footprint (git status --short):
   M .swiftlint.yml
   M project.yml
   ?? TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/
(no dashboard-widgets, no feature-views, no AIRestorePanel files touched.)

A) Co-located *.Tests.swift `import XCTest` compiled into the APP target:
   The established convention puts every surface's `<Name>.Tests.swift` (import XCTest +
   @testable import TeslaSync) in the app-target source dirs (feature-views, and now
   shared-surfaces). xcodebuild builds the app target without XCTest framework search
   paths, so EVERY such file fails `unable to resolve module dependency: 'XCTest'`
   (e.g. AIRestorePanel.Tests.swift, a pre-existing file). Fix is an integration-level
   decision (set ENABLE_TESTING_SEARCH_PATHS=YES on the app targets — verified to clear
   the errors — or move *.Tests.swift into the unit-test targets). Out of scope for a
   single surface prompt whose allowed files are shared-surfaces/ChartHiddenSeriesContext.*.

B) Duplicate public types across dashboard-widgets (parallel-merge collision):
   `public struct DashboardWidgetSize` and `public struct DashboardWidgetRegistration`
   are each declared in 10+ committed, unmodified files (UptimeMonitorWidget.Model.swift,
   TelemetryErrorsWidget.Model.swift, MQTTStatusWidget.Model.swift, VehicleHeroWidget.Model.swift,
   DigitalTwinWidget.Model.swift, …) → "invalid redeclaration" / "ambiguous type lookup".
   Fixing requires de-duplicating other surfaces' files — explicitly out of scope.

